ows</span> <h1>Structure process and documentation workflows clearly</h1> <p>When ERP, emails, files, records and specialist software run side by side, friction grows. IBS-Saxony makes visible which work steps, data sources, documents and responsibilities are involved today and which next operational step can bring relief.</p> <a class="button button-gold" href="/en/contact">Free initial call</a> </div> <aside class="process-flow-panel"> <span><strong>01</strong>Make system silos visible</span><span><strong>02</strong>Find records faster</span><span><strong>03</strong>Clarify approvals and responsibilities</span> </aside> </div> </section> <section class="section section-soft"> <div class="container"> <div class="section-heading"> <span class="section-kicker">Starting point</span> <h2>When documents travel, friction often grows.</h2> <p>Teams often lose time not because of one large weakness, but because of many small breaks: data is maintained twice, records are searched manually, approvals get stuck or new tools do not fit the real workday.</p> </div> <div class="card-grid three"> <article class="service-card"><span class="card-index">SY</span><h3>System silos</h3><p>Information lives in several systems. This creates duplicate entry, inconsistent data and repeated questions.</p></article><article class="service-card"><span class="card-index">MA</span><h3>Manual search</h3><p>Records, files and figures are gathered by hand. Responsibilities are not always clear.</p></article><article class="service-card"><span class="card-index">SO</span><h3>Software mismatch</h3><p>New digital tools help little when they do not fit the actual workflow, team and documentation need.</p></article> </div> </div> </section> <section class="section section-process-docs"> <div class="container"> <div class="section-heading"> <span class="section-kicker">Approach</span> <h2>From friction point to the next actionable workflow</h2> <p>The entry point stays deliberately small: we review one real workflow, separate quick improvements from topics needing further specialist review and prepare the next operational step.</p> </div> <div class="step-grid process-docs-steps"> <article class="step-card"><span>1</span><h3>Review workflows</h3><p>We capture which work steps, systems, documents and data sources are involved today.</p></article><article class="step-card"><span>2</span><h3>Prioritize bottlenecks</h3><p>We mark search time, duplicate entry, unclear handovers and points where specialist review may be needed.</p></article><article class="step-card"><span>3</span><h3>Prepare implementation</h3><p>You receive one clear next measure: workflow change, document structure, interface, template or project plan.</p></article> </div> </div> </section> <section class="section section-soft"> <div class="container"> <div class="section-heading"> <span class="section-kicker">Outcome</span> <h2>What becomes tangible</h2> </div> <div class="card-grid four"> <article class="service-card"><span class="card-index">01</span><h3>Workflow map</h3><p>A clear overview of who needs what and when, where data is created and where documents move.</p></article><article class="service-card"><span class="card-index">02</span><h3>Document structure</h3><p>An order for files, records, approvals and recurring documents that need to be found in daily work.</p></article><article class="service-card"><span class="card-index">03</span><h3>Roles and handovers</h3><p>Clear operational responsibilities to reduce questions, waiting time and duplicate maintenance.</p></article><article class="service-card"><span class="card-index">04</span><h3>Next work block</h3><p>One small actionable measure with goal, scope and price range before any paid start.</p></article> </div> </div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="container"> <div class="section-heading"> <span class="section-kicker">Focus</span> <h2>Especially useful for</h2> </div> <div class="card-grid three"> <article class="ser